// orthography does NOT determine: TONE (H á / L à — Mooré tone is contextual, unwritten → we emit none), SYLLABLE
// dots, and the geminate notation (CC ~ Cː). Vowel quality/length (⟨ɛ ɩ ʋ⟩, doubling) and NASALISATION (tilde) ARE
// written and emitted, so they are compared directly — NOT folded.
